{"html":"<p>A student of <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"socrates\">Socrates</a>, who wrote dialogues in which Socrates is usually the main speaker. Around 387 BCE he founded the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"platonic-academy\">Academy</a> in <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"athens\">Athens</a>. His <i>Republic</i> asks what justice is and imagines a city ruled by philosophers; Aristotle was his student for twenty years.</p>","links":["socrates","platonic-academy","athens"],"sum":"A student of Socrates, who wrote dialogues in which Socrates is usually the main speaker. Around 387 BCE he founded the Academy in Athens. His Republic asks what justice is and imagines a city ruled by philosophers; Aristotle was his studen…","rel":{"where":["athens"]},"back":["al-farabi","alcibiades","aristophanes","aristotle","aspasia","athens","athens-golden-age","athens-schools-closed","bessarion","council-of-florence","dionysius-i-of-syracuse","eleatic-school","epicureanism","gemistos-plethon","greek-teachers-in-italy","helike-swallowed-by-the-sea","hippocrates","homer","michael-psellos","minoan-eruption-of-thera","neoplatonism","platonic-academy","plotinuss-enneads","pythagoras","pythagoreanism","sappho","socrates","sophists","symposium","the-clouds","thirty-tyrants","trial-of-socrates"],"life":[{"y":-428,"h":"Born","c":1},{"y":-423,"h":"<a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"the-clouds\">The Clouds</a>","k":"the-clouds"},{"y":-404,"h":"<a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"thirty-tyrants\">Thirty Tyrants</a>","e":-403,"k":"thirty-tyrants"},{"y":-399,"h":"<a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"trial-of-socrates\">Trial of Socrates</a>","k":"trial-of-socrates"},{"y":-387,"h":"Around 387 BCE he founded the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"platonic-academy\">Academy</a> in <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"athens\">Athens</a>.","k":"platonic-academy"},{"y":-373,"h":"<a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"helike-swallowed-by-the-sea\">Helike swallowed by the sea</a>","k":"helike-swallowed-by-the-sea"},{"y":-347,"h":"Died"}]}